CHAPTER I GENERAL PROVISIONS

Article 1 (Purpose) The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters mandated by the Police Officials Act regarding the promotion of police officials and matters necessary for the enforcement thereof.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 2 (Relationship to other statutes or regulations) Except as otherwise expressly provided in other statutes or regulations, this Decree shall apply to the promotion of police officials (excluding police officers affiliated with the Korea Coast Guard; hereinafter the same shall apply). <Amended on Jun. 23, 2020>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 3 (Classification of promotion) The promotion of police officials shall be classified into promotion through review, promotion through examination, and special promotion.

Article 4 (Determination of number of persons eligible for promotion) (1) The Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency shall determine the number of persons to be promoted by rank, taking into account the actual vacancies at the time of determination and the expected vacancies for the relevant year; provided, where deemed necessary, the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency may determine the number of persons to be promoted by field (hereinafter referred to as "special field") based on the unique characteristics, etc. of duties. <Amended on Nov. 19, 2014; Oct. 31, 2016; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020>
  (2) The number of persons to be promoted to Superintendent General shall not exceed 25 percent of the fixed number of Superintendent Generals, and the number of persons to be promoted to Senior Superintendent shall not exceed 20 percent of the fixed number of Senior Superintendents from among the number of persons to be promoted under paragraph (1); provided, where the number of persons to be promoted to Superintendent General is less than the sum of the actual vacancies as at the time of determining the number of persons to be promoted and the estimated vacancies for the relevant year, the number of persons to be promoted may be determined by adding the shortfall to the number of persons to be promoted. <Amended on Oct. 31, 2016>
  (3) When determining the number of persons scheduled for promotion to Superintendent or lower ranks from among those scheduled for promotion under paragraph (1), a separate number may be determined for special promotion within the following limits; provided, in cases of special promotion falling under Article 37 (1) 1 and 4 and (3) 1 and 6, the number may exceed the limits: <Amended on Nov. 19, 2014; Oct. 31, 2016; Aug. 22, 2023>
  1. The number of persons to be promoted to Superintendent: Up to 3 percent of the number of persons to be promoted to Superintendent;
  2. The number of persons to be promoted to Senior Inspector or lower ranks: Up to 30 percent of the number of persons to be promoted to the relevant rank.
  (4) In cases of promotion to Superintendent or lower rank or Assistant Inspector or higher rank, promotion through a promotion review (hereinafter referred to as "promotion through review") and promotion through a promotion examination (hereinafter referred to as "promotion through examination") may be concurrently conducted in accordance with the proviso of Article 15 (2) of the Police Officials Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Act"); in such cases, the number of persons scheduled for promotion shall be determined by the following methods: <Amended on Oct. 31, 2016; Sep. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020; Dec. 31, 2020; Aug. 22, 2023>
  1. By rank, 70 percent of the total number of persons scheduled for promotion after subtracting those scheduled for special promotion under paragraph (3) shall be allocated for promotion through review, and the remaining 30 percent allocated for promotion through examination; provided, where the number of persons scheduled for promotion in a special field is determined pursuant to the proviso of paragraph (1), the ratio of the number of persons scheduled for promotion through review to the number of persons scheduled for promotion through examination under the main clause shall be adjusted accordingly:
  2. Notwithstanding subparagraph 1, if the promotion examination is conducted before the promotion review, and if the number of persons who have passed the final examination is less than the number of persons scheduled for promotion through examination, the shortfall shall be added to the number of persons scheduled for promotion through review.
  (5) The Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency shall allocate the number of persons scheduled for promotion determined pursuant to paragraphs (1) through (4) to each agency which has prepared a list of persons eligible for promotion pursuant to Article 11 (1). <Amended on Nov. 19, 2014; Oct. 31, 2016; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020>
  (6) The allocation of the number of persons under paragraph (5) shall be based on the ratio of persons recorded on the list of persons eligible for promotion in each agency; provided, adjustments may be made taking into account the conditions of promotion for each affiliated agency such as the number of persons scheduled for promotion for continuous service to the relevant rank. <Amended on Oct. 31, 2016>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]
  [Title Amended on Oct. 31, 2016]

Article 5 (Minimum number of service years required for promotion) (1) If a police official intends to be promoted, he or she shall have served in the relevant rank for a period classified as follows: <Amended on Jan. 3, 2023>
  1. Senior Superintendents: At least 3 years;
  2. Superintendents and Senior Inspectors: At least 2 years;
  3. Inspectors, Assistant Inspectors, Senior Police Officers, and Police Officers: At least 1 year.
  (2) Periods of leave of absence, release from position, disciplinary action, and periods of restriction on promotion under Article 6 (1) 2 shall not be included in the period under paragraph (1); provided, the following periods shall be included in the period under paragraph (1): <Amended on Apr. 25, 2017; Sep. 18, 2018; Nov. 20, 2018; Aug. 31, 2021; Jan. 24, 2025>
  1. The following periods during a leave of absence under Article 71 of the State Public Officials Act:
    (a) Where a public official takes a leave of absence pursuant to Article 71 (1) 1 of the State Public Officials Act due to a disease or injury sustained in the line of duty under the Public Officials' Accident Compensation Act, the period of leave of absence;
    (b) Where a public official takes a leave of absence pursuant to Article 71 (1) 3 or 5 or 71 (2) 1 of the State Public Officials Act, the period of such leave of absence;
    (c) Where a public official takes a leave of absence pursuant to Article 71 (2) 2 of the State Public Officials Act, 50 percent of the period of leave of absence;
    (d) Where a public official takes a leave of absence pursuant to Article 71 (2) 4 of the State Public Officials Act (hereinafter referred to as "child care leave"), the period of such leave of absence; provided, the period included in the period under paragraph (1), combined with the period of service during which the public official was designated and served as a public official converted to part-time service in lieu of child care leave under paragraph (6) 3, shall not exceed 3 years per child;
  2. In any of the following cases, the period during which he or she is released from his or her position:
    (a) Where the competent disciplinary committee decides not to take a disciplinary action against a person who has been subject to a release from his or her position pursuant to Article 73-3 (1) 3 of the State Public Officials Act, and where the disciplinary action leading to the release from position is invalidated or revoked by a decision of the appeals review committee or a court judgment;
    (b) Where a person who was subjected to release from position pursuant to Article 73-3 (1) 4 of the State Public Officials Act is found not guilty in a criminal case that was the basis for release from the position through the decision of the court:
    (c) Where any misconduct (hereinafter referred to as "misconduct") which is a cause for disposition against a person who was subjected to release from position under Article 73-3 (1) 6 of the State Public Officials Act falls under both (i) and (ii):
    (i) In any of the following cases in relation to disciplinary procedures for misconduct:
    (ii) Where the results of an inspection or investigation of a misconduct fall under any of the following cases:
  (3) The period during which a person appointed as an inspector after graduating from the Korean National Police University served as a member of an auxiliary police company pursuant to Article 2-3 (2) of the Act on the Establishment and Operation of Auxiliary Police Companies shall not be included in the period prescribed in paragraph (1). <Amended on Oct. 31, 2016>
  (4) If a person employed as a police official pursuant to Article 10 (3) 4 of the Act has previously served as a public official of Grade V or higher (including a public official in special service corresponding thereto) for at least 5 years before his or her employment, he or she shall be deemed to have served during the period equivalent to 20 percent of such period he or she held at the time of employment and the period shall count toward that referred to in paragraph (1). <Amended on Jun. 12, 2018; Dec. 31, 2020>
  (5) The training period as a judicial trainee under Article 72 of the Court Organization Act shall be included in the minimum number of years of service required for promotion to Superintendent or lower-ranking police officials under paragraph (1).
  (6) For police officials working shorter hours than the ordinary working hours under Article 26-2 of the State Public Officials Act and Article 57-3 of the Decree on the Appointment of Public Officials (hereinafter referred to as "police official converted to part-time service"), their period of service shall be included in the period referred to in paragraph (1) in accordance with the following standards: <Amended on Jun. 12, 2018; Sep. 18, 2018; Jan. 24, 2025>
  1. The entire period of up to 1 year during which he or she served as a police officer converted to part-time service at the relevant rank;
  2. Any period exceeding 1 year during which he or she served as a police officer converted to part-time service at the relevant rank, calculated in proportion to the service hours;
  3. The entire period of up to 3 years per child during which he or she was designated and served as a police official converted to part-time service in lieu of child care leave at the relevant rank.
  (7) If a demoted person is later promoted back to the rank he or she held immediately before the demotion, the service period in the rank immediately before the demotion shall be included in the period referred to in paragraph (1).
  (8) In the event of a demotion, the service period in the rank immediately preceding the demotion shall be included in the period referred to in paragraph (1).
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 6 (Restrictions on promotion) (1) A police official who falls under any of the following subparagraphs shall not be eligible for promotion: <Amended on Sep. 22, 2015; Sep. 18, 2018; Dec. 11, 2018; Nov. 5, 2019; Dec. 31, 2020>
  1. A person who is currently under a request for a resolution on disciplinary action, undergoing disciplinary action, released from his or her position, leave of absence (excluding cases where a person who has taken a leave of absence pursuant to Article 71 (1) 1 of the State Public Officials Act due to a disease or injury incurred during the performance of his or her duties under the Public Officials' Accident Compensation Act is specially appointed pursuant to Article 37 (1) 4 or 37 (2) of that Article) or a person who is in a probationary appointment period;
  2. A person for whom the following periods [an additional 6 months shall be added in cases of disciplinary disposition due to a cause falling under any of the subparagraphs of Article 78-2 (1) of the State Public Officials Act and disciplinary disposition for passive administration, drunk driving (including where a person refuses to take a breath test), sexual violence, sexual harassment, or sexual trafficking] have not elapsed from the date of completion of disciplinary action:
    (a) Demotion and suspension from office: 18 months;
    (b) Salary reduction: 12 months;
    (c) Reprimand: 6 months;
  3. A person appointed as a police official after serving as a public official subject to other statutes or regulations with respect to disciplinary action, and for whom the periods falling under the following have not passed since the date he or she became subject to disciplinary action in the former status and such action was completed:
    (a) Demotion: 18 months;
    (b) Probation, detention in a guardhouse, or other similar disciplinary measures: 6 months;
  4. A person whose rank retirement age has been extended pursuant to Article 30 (3) of the Act.
  (2) If a person under restriction on promotion under paragraph (1) is subject to disciplinary action again, the period of restriction on promotion shall be calculated from the expiration date of the current restriction period, and if a person under restriction on promotion for a previous disciplinary action is subject to a disciplinary action, the remaining period of restriction on promotion shall be calculated from the date of reinstatement. <Amended on Aug. 22, 2023>
  (3) If a police official receives any of the following awards while serving in the relevant rank after he or she is subject to disciplinary action, the period of restriction on promotion under paragraph (1) 2 and 3 may be reduced by 1/2: <Amended on Jun. 12, 2018>
  1. Decorations;
  2. Medals;
  3. Awards for exemplary public officials;
  4. Presidential citations or the prime minister's citations;
  5. Awards received for adopting and implementing a proposal.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

CHAPTER II EVALUATION OF POLICE OFFICIALS

Article 7 (Evaluation of work performance records) (1) The work performance records of Senior Superintendents and lower-ranking police officials shall be evaluated annually, and the results of these evaluations shall be used for personnel management purposes, such as promotions. <Amended on Oct. 31, 2016>
  (2) Work performance records shall be evaluated based on the following evaluation criteria; provided, the work performance records of Senior Superintendents shall be evaluated based only on the second evaluation elements: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Nov. 19, 2014; Oct. 31, 2016; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020>
  1. 1st evaluation elements:
    (a) Contribution to the advancement of police duties;
    (b) Awards received;
    (c) Other evaluation elements prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety;
  2. 2nd evaluation elements:
    (a) Work experience;
    (b) Ability to perform duties;
    (c) Attitude toward the performance of duties.
  (3) The evaluation of work performance based on the second evaluation elements shall be such that the evaluation results for each rank of persons subject to evaluation meet the distribution ratios falling under each of the following subparagraphs; provided, where no person falls under subparagraph 4 as a result of the evaluation, the ratio allocated under subparagraph 4 shall be added to the ratio under subparagraph 3: <Amended on Oct. 31, 2016>
  1. Grade A: 20 percent;
  2. Grade B: 40 percent;
  3. Grade C: 30 percent;
  4. Grade D: 10 percent.
  (4) When evaluating police officials falling under the proviso of Article 11 (2) and Inspectors directly handling investigations into complaints, accusations, etc. within the investigation division of a police station, the ratios referred to in paragraph (3) need not be applied.
  (5) The results of the work performance evaluation shall not be disclosed; provided, the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency may, upon the completion of evaluations, notify the police officials subject to the evaluation of their evaluation results. <Amended on Nov. 20, 2018; Jun. 23, 2020>
  (6) The standards, timing, methods, and other necessary matters for the evaluation of work performance records shall be prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Interior and Safety. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Nov. 19, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 8 (Exceptions to evaluation of work performance records) (1) A police official who has not served for at least 6 months at the evaluation agency during the relevant year, due to reasons such as a leave of absence or release from position, shall not be subject to the evaluation of work performance records.
  (2) Deleted. <Oct. 31, 2016>
  (3) A police official who has been dispatched to a State agency, a local government, or an agency designated by the Minister of Personnel Management for at least 2 months, for reasons other than education and training, shall be evaluated with consideration given to the opinions of the agency to which he or she has been dispatched. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Nov. 19, 2014>
  (4) If a police official who is subject to evaluation is transferred, his or her work performance evaluation records shall be transferred to the agency to which he or she has been transferred; provided, where a regular evaluation is conducted within 2 months after the transfer, the work performance records for the service period before the transfer shall be evaluated by the original agency and then transferred, and the new agency shall conduct an evaluation based on the evaluation results received from the previous agency.
  (5) For police officials newly hired or promoted after a regular evaluation, their work performance records shall be evaluated after they have completed 2 months of service in their new positions.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 9 (Career evaluation) (1) The career evaluation of police officials shall be conducted based on the number of years of service of Senior Superintendents or lower-ranking police officials (excluding those falling under the proviso of Article 11 (2)) who have completed the minimum number of service years required for promotion under Article 5, and the results of the career evaluation shall be reflected in the preparation of the list of persons eligible for promotion.
  (2) Career evaluation shall be conducted based on the personnel records of the relevant police officials, and where deemed necessary, the accuracy of these records may be verified through inquiries. <Amended on Jun. 12, 2018>
  (3) Career evaluation shall be classified into basic and excess career, and the periods included in each category by rank shall be as follows: <Amended on Sep. 22, 2015; Jun. 23, 2020; Jan. 3, 2023; Aug. 22, 2023>
  1. Basic career:
    (a) Senior Superintendent, Superintendent, and Senior Inspector: The last 3 years from the base date of evaluation;
    (b) Inspector and Assistant Inspector: The last 2 years from the base date of evaluation;
    (c) Senior Police Officer and Police Officer: The last 1 year and 6 months from the base date of evaluation;
  2. Excess career:
    (a) Senior Superintendent: 1 year prior to the basic career;
    (c) Inspector: 3 years prior to the basic career period;
    (a) Senior Superintendent: 1 year prior to the basic career period;
    (d) Assistant Inspector: 1 year prior to the basic career period;
    (e) Senior Police Officer and Police Officer: 6 months prior to the basic career period.
  (4) The timing, methods, and calculation of the period of career evaluation, and other necessary matters shall be prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Nov. 19, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 10 Deleted. <Dec. 9, 2014>

CHAPTER III LIST OF PERSONS ELIGIBLE FOR PROMOTION

Article 11 (Preparation of list of persons eligible for promotion) (1) The list of Senior Superintendent or lower-ranking police officials eligible for promotion shall be prepared by the head of each police agency classified as follows (hereinafter referred to as "person responsible for preparing the promotion list") by rank: <Amended on Mar. 30, 2018; Dec. 31, 2020>
  1. Superintendent or higher-ranking police officials and Inspector or higher-ranking police officials at the Korean National Police Agency: Prepared by the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency;
  2. Senior Inspector or lower-ranking police officials (excluding persons falling under subparagraph 4): Prepared by the heads of the Korean National Police University, the Police Human Resources Development Institute, the Central Police Academy, the Korean Police Investigation Academy, a police hospital, or a City/Do police agency (hereinafter referred to as "affiliated agencies, etc.");
  3. Assistant Inspector or lower-ranking police officials at the Korean National Police Agency: Prepared by the head of each department at the director-general level within each bureau of the Korean National Police Agency;
  4. Assistant Inspector or lower-ranking police officials affiliated with a police station: Prepared by the chief of a police station.
  (2) The list of persons eligible for promotion shall be prepared by reflecting the evaluation points calculated pursuant to Articles 7 through 9 as classified in the following subparagraphs; provided, the list for newly employed Superintendents or lower-ranking police officials pursuant to Article 10 (3) 2 or 4 of the Act and who are within the age limit for examination under Article 39 (1) of the Decree on the Appointment of Police Officials, may be prepared based only on work performance evaluation until promotion to Superintendent: <Amended on Dec. 9, 2014; Oct. 31, 2016; Dec. 30, 2016; Dec. 30, 2016; Dec. 31, 2020>
  1. Evaluation points for work performance records: 65 percent;
  2. Career evaluation points: 35 percent;
  3. Deleted. <Dec. 9, 2014>
  (3) Deleted. <Dec. 19, 2023>
  (4) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency shall prepare a list of persons eligible for promotion under subparagraph 1, and the commissioner of a City/Do police agency shall compile a list of persons eligible for promotion under subparagraph 2 by rank, but the final consolidated list shall align the order of candidates according to their total evaluation points: <Amended on Oct. 31, 2016; Dec. 31, 2020>
  1. Promotion to Inspector or lower rank belonging to the Korean National Police Agency: A list of persons eligible for promotion prepared by the head of each department at the director-general level of the Korean National Police Agency;
  2. Promotion to Inspector or lower rank under the proviso of Article 17 (1): A list of persons eligible for promotion prepared by the commissioner of a City/Do police agency or the chief of a police station.
  (5) A person responsible for preparing the promotion list may, if necessary, prepare separate lists by police branch or special field. <Amended on Oct. 31, 2016>
  (6) The list of persons eligible for promotion shall be prepared as of January 1 of each year; provided, for promotions to Superintendent General and Senior Superintendent, the list shall be prepared as of November 1 of each year.
  (7) Deleted. <Jun. 23, 2020>
  (8) Except as provided in this Decree, details necessary for preparing a list of persons eligible for promotion shall be prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety. <Added on Oct. 31, 2016; Jul. 26, 2017>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 12 Deleted. <Oct. 31, 2016>

Article 13 (Adjustment of list of persons eligible for promotion) A person responsible for preparing the promotion list shall adjust the list if any of the following circumstances arise after such list has been prepared:
  1. Where a person is transferred to or from an agency;
  2. Deleted; <Dec. 9, 2014>
  3. Where a person becomes subject to disciplinary action or is released from his or her position;
  4. Where his or her career is re-evaluated due to reasons such as discrepancies found between the facts and the initial evaluation;
  5. Where a person goes on leave of absence or a retires;
  6. Where a person falls under the period of restriction on promotion under Article 6 (1) 2 through 4.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

CHAPTER IV PROMOTION REVIEW

Article 14 (Promotion review) (1) The promotion review for police officials shall be conducted by rank, but if deemed necessary by the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency, the review may be conducted either by rank or by special field. <Amended on Nov. 19, 2014; Oct. 31, 2016; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020>
  (2) The promotion review for ranks up to Superintendent or lower shall be conducted once a year between January 2 and March 31; provided, where the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency deems that the review cannot be completed within such period, the period may be extended; and if there is an increase in the number of police officials or any other special reason exists, additional promotion reviews may be conducted. <Amended on Nov. 19, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 15 (Composition of the Central Promotion Review Committee) (1) The Central Promotion Review Committee under Article 17 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Central Promotion Review Committee") shall consist of at least 5 but not more than 7 members, including the chairperson. <Amended on Dec. 31, 2020>
  (2) Multiple Promotion Deliberation Committees may be established in the Central Promotion Review Committee to deliberate in advance on matters to be submitted to the meetings of the Central Promotion Review Committee, and each Promotion Deliberation Committee shall consist of at least 5 but not more than 7 members.
  (3) Deleted. <Jun. 23, 2020>
  (4) Members referred to in paragraphs (1) and (2) shall be appointed by the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency from among police officials who hold a rank higher than those subject to promotion review before the date of the committee's meeting, but if a Promotion Deliberation Committee is established pursuant to paragraph (2), members of the Central Promotion Review Committee shall be appointed from among the members of the Promotion Deliberation Committee. <Amended on Nov. 19, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020>
  (5) Notwithstanding paragraph (4), the members of the Central Promotion Review Committee convened to deliberate on whether to grant special promotion under Article 37 (2), whether to revoke such promotion under Article 40-2 (3) 3, and whether to ratify such promotion after appointment under the latter part of Article 41 (2) shall be as follows; in such cases, a majority of the members shall be those referred to in subparagraph 2: <Added on Jul. 7, 2025>
  1. A police official of a higher rank than the person subject to special promotion review (including public officials holding equivalent ranks or members of the Senior Executive Service; hereafter in this subparagraph the same shall apply) as designated by the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency; provided, where there is a shortage of police officials of a higher rank than the person subject to special promotion review, a police official of the same rank designated by the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency may also be included;
  2. Any of the following persons commissioned by the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency:
    (a) A person who has served as a judge, public prosecutor, or attorney-at-law for at least 10 years;
    (b) A person who has served as an assistant professor or higher at a university for at least 10 years;
    (c) A person who has expertise in personnel affairs, labor affairs, or police-related affairs, or who has worked in a related field for at least 10 years.
  (6) The chairperson referred to in paragraph (5) shall be the police official of the highest rank or the senior police official among the members, and the chairperson referred to in paragraph (5) 2 shall be appointed by the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency from among the members referred to in paragraph (5) 2. <Amended on Jul. 7, 2025>
  (7) A member referred to in paragraph (5) shall be excluded from review by the Central Promotion Review Committee in any of the following cases: <Added on Jul. 7, 2025>
  1. Where the member is or was a relative (referring to a relative under Article 777 of the Civil Act) of the person subject to review in the relevant case;
  2. Where the member is involved in a fact constituting a requirement for special promotion subject to review in the relevant case or for the revocation thereof; provided, this shall not apply where the public official is involved in such fact in the performance of his or her duties.
  (8) Where a member referred to in paragraph (5) falls under any ground for exclusion prescribed in the subparagraphs of paragraph (7) or where the circumstances indicate that it would be impracticable to expect fair reviews by himself or herself, the member may recuse himself or herself from the review of the relevant agenda item. <Added on Jul. 7, 2025>
  (9) Except as provided in paragraphs (1), (2), and (4) through (8), matters necessary for the operation of the Promotion Deliberation Committee shall be prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Nov. 19, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020; Jul. 7, 2025>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 16 (Composition of general promotion review committee) (1) A general promotion review committee under Article 17 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "general promotion review committee") shall be established in the Korean National Police Agency, its affiliated agencies, etc., and police stations. <Amended on Nov. 5, 2013; Nov. 19, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020; Dec. 31, 2020>
  (2) A general promotion review committee shall consist of at least 5, but less than 7 members, including 1 chairperson.
  (3) Members of the general promotion review committee shall be appointed by the head of the police agency where the committee is established, from among Inspectors or police officials holding ranks higher than those subject to promotion review, and the chairperson shall be the highest-ranking police official or the most senior police official among the members. <Amended on Nov. 20, 2018>
  (4) Notwithstanding paragraph (3), 2 of the members of a general promotion review committee established in a City/Do police agency and a police station shall be Inspector or hold a higher rank than those subject to the review and shall be appointed by the head of the police agency upon the recommendations of the Si/Do autonomous police committee under Article 18 (1) of the Act on the Organization and Operation of National Police and Autonomous Police. <Added on 31, Dec. 31, 2020>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 17 (Jurisdiction of promotion review committee) (1) A promotion review committee shall be responsible for reviewing the promotion of police officials based on the following classifications; provided, the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency may, if unavoidable in consideration of the number of persons to be promoted, etc., have the general promotion review committee in a City/Do police agency conduct reviews for promotions to Inspector or lower ranks, which may typically be handled by a general promotion review committee in a police station as part of promotion review under subparagraph 2. <Amended on Dec. 31, 2020>
  1. Review for promotion to Senior Superintendent or higher: The review conducted by the Central Promotion Review Committee;
  2. Review for promotion to Superintendent or lower: The review conducted by a general promotion review committee at the police agency to which the relevant police officer belongs (excluding cases falling under subparagraph 3);
  3. Review for promotion of police officers at a police station to Senior Inspector or higher: The review conducted by a general promotion review committee in the City/Do police agency.
  (2) Deleted. <Jun. 23, 2020>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 18 (Meetings of promotion review committee) (1) Meetings of the Central Promotion Review Committee shall be convened by the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency, and meetings of a general promotion review committee shall be convened by the head of the relevant police agency with approval from the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency (in cases of a meeting of the general promotion review committee in a police station, referring to the Commissioner General of a City/Do police agency). <Amended on Dec. 31, 2020>
  (2) Any resolution of a promotion review committee shall require the concurring vote of a majority of the members present at the meeting.
  (3) Meetings of a promotion review committee shall be closed to the public.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 19 (Executive secretary of promotion review committee) (1) Each promotion review committee shall have 1 executive secretary and several clerks.
  (2) The executive secretary and clerks shall be appointed by the head of the relevant police agency from among police officials in charge of personnel affairs within the police agency where the promotion review committee is established.
  (3) The executive secretary shall handle the committee's affairs according to the chairperson's directives, and the clerks shall assist the executive secretary with its affairs.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 20 (Persons subject to review for promotion) The promotion review shall be conducted in order of priority (excluding persons who have passed the examination for promotion) from the list of persons eligible for promotion under Article 11, and shall be applied to 5 times the number of persons scheduled for promotion through review; provided, if there is any unavoidable cause, the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency may limit the number of persons subject to review to 5 times the number of those scheduled for promotion through review. <Amended on November 19, 2014, on October 31, 2016, on July 26, 2017, on June 23, 2020>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 21 (Exclusion from promotion review) If a police official falls under any of the following, he or she will be excluded from review for promotion: <Amended on Sep. 17, 2013; Jun. 12, 2018; Dec. 10, 2024>
  1. Where he or she fails to complete the education under subparagraph 1 of Appendix 1 of the Regulations on the Education and Training of Police Officials or where his or her educational performance is below 60 percent of the perfect score;
  2. Where he or she falls under any subparagraph of Article 6 (1);
  3. Deleted; <Jun. 12, 2018>
  4. Where Senior Superintendent or a lower-ranking police official fails to meet the required hours of education and training necessary for promotion under Article 6 (1) of the Regulations on the Education and Training of Police Officials; provided, this shall not apply to cases falling under Article 6 (2) 1 of the Regulations on the Education and Training of Police Officials.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 22 (Criteria for promotion review) (1) A promotion review committee shall examine the following matters to determine whether a person subject to review for promotion has the ability to perform duties associated with the rank to which he or she is to be promoted: <Amended on Oct. 31, 2016>
  1. Positions held;
  2. Promotion history;
  3. Annual work performance in the current rank;
  4. Rewards and punishments;
  5. Evaluation and recommendation by the heads of the relevant police agency;
  6. Aptitude.
  (2) The procedures for promotion review and other necessary matters shall be prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Nov. 19, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 22-2 (Reflection of results of peer and civil petitioner evaluations) (1) When an appointing authority (including those delegated with the authority to appoint police officials pursuant to Article 4 (1) through (6) of the Decree on the Appointment of Police Officials; hereinafter the same shall apply) or appointment-recommendation authority (including the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency where recommendation under Article 7 (1) of the Act is required; hereinafter the same shall apply) promotes or recommends the promotion of police officials under his or her jurisdiction through promotion review, he or she may conduct an evaluation by peers and civil petitioners of those subject to review and reflect the results thereof. In such cases, peer evaluations shall be conducted by police officials of the higher, same, or lower ranks of the person subject to promotion, and civil petitioner evaluations shall be conducted by civil petitioners, etc. related to the duties of the person subject to promotion review. <Amended on Nov. 19, 2014; Dec. 30, 2016; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 12, 2018; June. 23, 2020; Dec. 31, 2020>
  (2) The results of these evaluations under paragraph (1) may be reflected in various aspects of personnel management, such as special promotion, payment of performance-based bonuses, education and training, and management of positions.
  (3) Matters regarding the implementation of the evaluations, the reflection of the evaluation results in personnel management under paragraphs (1) and (2), and other relevant matters shall be determined by the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency. <Amended on Nov. 19, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 23 (Reporting on results of promotion review) (1) Upon completing a promotion review, a promotion review committee completes shall, without delay, prepare the following documents and report them to the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency for the Central Promotion Review Committee, and to the head of a police agency where the committee is established for a general promotion review committee: <Amended on Nov. 19, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 12, 2018; Jun. 23, 2020>
  1. A written resolution of the promotion review;
  2. A comprehensive evaluation report on the promotion review;
  3. A list of persons selected for promotion.
  (2) The list of persons selected for promotion under paragraph (1) 3 shall be prepared in the order of those who have excellent results in the comprehensive evaluation of promotion reviews, and in the event of a tie, priority shall be determined in the order prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety. <Amended on Oct. 31, 2016; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 12, 2018>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]
  [Title Amended on Oct. 31, 2016]

Article 24 (Preparation of list of candidates for promotion through review) (1) The appointing authority or the appointment-recommendation authority shall prepare a list of candidates for promotion review for those who have been selected for promotion through review by a promotion review committee.
  (2) Article 23 (2) shall apply mutatis mutandis to the preparation of a list of candidates for promotion through review. <Amended on Jun. 12, 2018>
  (3) If a person recorded on the list of candidates for promotion through review becomes subject to a disciplinary action, such as suspension from office or a more severe penalty before the promotion, the appointing authority or appointment-recommendation authority shall remove such person from the list of candidates.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 25 (Promotion of candidates for promotion) (1) When promoting police officials, 70 percent of the total number of promotions shall be allocated to promotion through review, and 30 percent shall be allocated to promotion through examination. <Amended on Sep. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020; Aug. 22, 2023>
  (2) Promotions through review shall be made on an ad hoc basis whenever vacancies arise following the order recorded on the list of candidates for promotion through review under Article 24.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 26 (Promotion for continuous service) (1) The period required for promotion for continuous service under Article 16 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "promotion for continuous service") shall be calculated according to the method for calculating the minimum number of service years required for promotion under Article 5 (2) through (8). <Amended on Oct. 31, 2016; Dec. 31, 2020>
  (2) If the following police officials are promoted for continuous service pursuant to the proviso, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 16 (1) of the Act, the period classified as follows may be reduced from the promotion period for continuous service: <Added on Aug. 31, 2021>
  (2) If the following police officials are promoted for continuous service pursuant to the proviso, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 16 (1) of the Act, the periods classified as follows may be reduced from the promotion period for continuous service: <Added on Aug. 31, 2021>
  2. Police officials with an excellent track record in performing major duties, such as state affairs, or those with an outstanding attitude towards proactive administration: 1 year.
  (3) The Minister of Personnel Management may restrict the number of police officials whose period of promotion for continuous service is shortened pursuant to paragraph (2) 2. <Added on Aug. 31, 2021>
  (4) In conducting a review for promotion to Senior Inspector for continuous service, the appointing authority shall not promote more than 50/100 of the number of persons eligible for such promotion in the relevant agency, calculated on an annual aggregate basis (adding 1 person where there is a fractional remainder). <Amended on Jun. 27, 2024>
  (5) If the appointing authority intends to conduct a review pursuant to paragraph (4), he or she shall report to the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency the number of persons eligible for promotion for continuous service and the number of persons scheduled for such promotion in the relevant agency not later than 20 days before the date of the promotion. <Added on Oct. 11, 2022; Jun. 27, 2024>
  (6) If deemed necessary for a smooth personnel management, the appointing authority may prepare a list of persons eligible for promotion by service period as Inspectors, categorized accordingly. <Amended on Jun. 12, 2018; Aug. 31, 2021; Oct. 11, 2022>
  (7) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) through (6), the methods of promotion for continuous service and other matters necessary for the management of personnel affairs shall be determined by the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency <Amended on Nov. 19, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 12, 2018; Jun. 23, 2020; Aug. 31, 2021; Oct. 11, 2022>
  [This Article Added on Dec. 21, 2011]

CHAPTER V EXAMINATIONS FOR PROMOTION

Article 27 (Principles in conducting examinations) (1) The examinations for promotion of police officials (hereinafter referred to as "examination") shall be conducted by rank, but if deemed necessary by the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency, the examinations may be conducted by police branch or by special field. <Amended on Nov. 19, 2014; Oct. 31, 2016; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020>
  (2) If an examination is conducted by police branch or special field pursuant to paragraph (1), the promotion may be contingent upon the person serving in a department designated by the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency for a period determined by the Minister of the Interior and Safety, which shall be at least 2 years but not more than 5 years following promotion. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Nov. 19, 2014; Oct. 31, 2016; Oct. 31, 2016; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 28 (Delegation of authority to conduct examinations) The Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency may delegate to the head of an affiliated agency, etc. an examination to Superintendent or lower ranks pursuant to Article 20 (1) of the Act. <Amended on Nov. 19, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020; Dec. 31, 2020; Dec. 19, 2023>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 29 (Qualifications for examination) A police official who intends to take an examination shall meet the following requirements: <Amended on Sep. 17, 2013; Jun. 12, 2018; Dec. 10, 2024>
  1. He or she shall have served in the relevant rank for at least the minimum number of service years required for promotion under Article 5 as of January 1 of the year in which the examination is conducted;
  2. He or she shall have completed the education under subparagraph 1 of Appendix 1 of the Regulations on the Education and Training of Police Officials (excluding basic management education and training for Senior Superintendents) with a score of at least 60 percent of the full mark;
  3. He or she shall not be subject to any of the grounds for restrictions on promotion under Article 6 (1);
  4. In the case of a Senior Superintendent or a lower-ranking police official, he or she shall have completed the required hours of education and training necessary for promotion under Article 6 (1) of the Regulations on the Education and Training of Police Officials; provided, this shall not apply to cases falling under Article 6 (2) 1 of the Regulations on the Education and Training of Police Officials.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 30 (Administration and public announcement of examinations) (1) Examinations shall be conducted once a year.
  (2) The date, time, venue, and place of the examination and other matters necessary for conducting the examination shall be publicly announced not later than 15 days before the examination.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 31 (Methods and procedures for examination) (1) The examination shall be conducted in 3 rounds with the following methods: <Amended on Nov. 19, 2014; Oct. 30, 2015; Oct. 31, 2016>
  1. The 1st round of examination shall primarily consist of multiple-choice questions, but fill-in-the-blank questions for each subject may be added; provided, where the examination is conducted by police branch or by special field, the practical examination may be conducted or included as an additional component;
  2. The 2nd round of examination shall primarily consist of thesis-type questions, but subjective short-answer questions for each subject may be added; provided, where the examination is conducted by police branch or by special field, the practical examination may be conducted or included as an additional component;
  3. The 3rd round of examination shall be an oral interview, during which the candidate's application ability and eligibility necessary for the performance of duties shall be assessed.
  (2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), if deemed necessary by the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency, the 3rd round of examination may be omitted, and the 1st and 2nd rounds of examination may be conducted simultaneously. <Amended on Nov. 19, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020>
  (3) If a person fails to pass the 1st round of examination, he or she shall not apply for the 2nd round of examination, and if he or she fails to pass the 2nd round, he or she shall not apply for the 3rd round; provided, this shall not apply where the 1st and 2nd rounds are conducted simultaneously under paragraph (2).
  (4) If the 1st and 2nd rounds of examination are conducted simultaneously pursuant to paragraph (2), the results of the 2nd round for a person who fails to pass the 1st round shall become null and void.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 31-2 (Special cases concerning examination methods for Senior Inspectors or lower ranks) (1) Notwithstanding Article 31 (1), examinations for the rank of Senior Inspector or lower, an examination may be divided into a written examination and an oral interview, focusing on special fields designated by the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency; provided, where deemed necessary by the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency, an oral interview may be omitted. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Nov. 19, 2014; Oct. 31, 2016; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020>
  (2) The written examination and oral interview under paragraph (1) shall be conducted as follows:
  1. The written examination shall primarily consist of multiple-choice questions, but fill-in-the-blank questions may be added for each subject;
  2. The oral interview shall be conducted to assess the candidate's application ability and eligibility necessary for the performance of duties.
  (3) If a person fails to pass the written examination, he or she shall not apply for the oral interview.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 32 (Examination subjects) The subjects of the 1st and 2nd rounds of examination under Article 31 (1) and the subjects for the written examination under Article 31-2 and the percentage of points allocated to each subject shall be prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Nov. 19, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 33 (Determination of success in examination) (1) In the 1st and 2nd rounds of examination, successful candidates shall be determined based on their total scores in all subjects, starting with the highest scores, considering the number of persons to be selected, among persons who score at least 40 percent of the perfect scores in each subject. <Amended on Oct. 31, 2016>
  (2) In the 3rd round of examination, candidates shall be assessed on a pass or fail basis only.
  (3) Persons passing the final examination shall be determined in order of score, starting with those who obtain the highest scores obtained by aggregating the following ratios from among those who have passed the 3rd round (referring to those who have passed the 2nd round if the 3rd round is not conducted): <Amended on Dec. 9, 2014; Oct. 31, 2016>
  1. Results of the 1st round of examination: 35 percent (30 percent in cases of the security police officer);
  1. Results of the 2nd round of examination: 24 percent (30 percent in cases of the security police officer);
  3. Results of work performance records in the relevant rank: 40 percent;
  4. Deleted. <Dec. 9, 2014>
  (4) The work performance records in the relevant rank under paragraph (3) 3 shall be calculated based on the evaluation points for the rank within the last 1 year from the base date of the examination year for Inspectors or lower-ranking police officials, and for Senior Inspectors or lower-ranking police officials, by the following calculation methods based on the evaluation points for the relevant rank within the last 2 years from the base date of the examination year: <Amended on Jun. 12, 2018; Aug. 22, 2023>
  (Evaluation points within the latest 1 year x 60/100) + (Evaluation points within the last 1 to 2 years x 40/100)
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 33-2 (Determination of success in special examination) (1) If an examination is conducted pursuant to Article 31-2, successful candidates in the written examination and oral interview shall be determined as follows: <Amended on Oct. 31, 2016>
  1. In the written examination, successful candidates shall be determined in the order of highest score, considering the number of persons to be selected, from among those who achieve scores at least 40 percent of the perfect score in each subject;
  2. In the oral interview, candidates shall be assessed on a pass or fail basis only.
  (2) The final successful candidates shall be determined in the order of highest score, from among those who have passed the oral interview (in cases where the interview is omitted according to the proviso of Article 31-2 (1), referring to those who have passed the written examination), calculated by aggregating the following ratios; in such cases, Article 33 (4) shall apply mutatis mutandis to the methods of calculating work performance in the relevant rank: <Amended on Dec. 9, 2014; Oct. 31, 2016>
  1. Results of the written examination: 60 percent;
  2. Results of work performance in the relevant rank: 40 percent;
  3. Deleted. <Dec. 9, 2014>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 33-3 (Method of calculating scores for elective subjects in special examinations) (1) Scores in elective subjects in the written examination under Article 31-2 shall be determined by calculating the standard deviation and the average scores in the subjects selected by applicants and adjusted according to the calculation formulate in the Appendix (hereinafter referred to as "adjusted scores").
  (2) "At least 40 percent of the perfect score in each subject" in Article 33-2 (1) 1 means either the adjusted score or the pre-adjusted score of the applicant at or above 40 percent.
  [This Article Added on Dec. 24, 2019]

Article 34 (Appointment of examiners) (1) The head of the agency conducting an examination may appoint or commission examiners to take charge of matters necessary for conducting the examination from among the following persons:
  1. A person with professional knowledge or expertise in the relevant field;
  2. A person familiar with the practical affairs related to the duties he or she is scheduled to assume.
  (2) Allowances shall be paid to examiners within the budget, as determined by the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency. <Amended on Nov. 19, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 35 (Measures against cheaters) (1) If a person commits any of the following acts during an examination, the examination shall be suspended or invalidated, or his or her passing scores shall be revoked, and he or she shall be prohibited from taking any examination under this Decree for 5 years from the date of such disposition:
  1. Viewing another examinee's answer sheet or allowing another to view his or her answer sheet;
  2. Requesting or taking an examination by proxy;
  3. Communicating with another person regarding the content of the relevant examination using communication devices, other signals, etc.;
  4. Possessing or using unauthorized materials;
  5. Taking prohibited drugs or using prohibited methods determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Personnel Management pursuant to Article 51 (1) 6 of the Decree on Public Officials Appointment Examinations for the purpose of influencing the practical examination;
  6. Engaging in any other act that affects the examination results of the person himself or herself or another person by improper means.
  (2) If a police official commits any of the following acts during an examination, the examination shall be suspended or invalidated:
  1. Viewing examination questions before the start of the examination;
  2. Preparing an answer sheet before the start and after the completion of the examination;
  3. Possessing unauthorized communication devices or electronic calculators;
  4. Committing other acts affecting the fair conduct of the examination, which are determined and publicly announced by the head of the institution conducting examinations as grounds for suspension or invalidation.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Nov. 20, 2018]

Article 36 (Preparation of list of candidates for promotion through examination) (1) The appointing authority or appointment-recommendation authority shall prepare a list of candidates for promotion by rank from those who have passed the examination in descending order of scores under Article 33-3 (3) or 33-2 (2). <Amended on Oct. 31, 2016>
  (2) Promotions through examination shall be conducted in the order listed in the list of candidates for promotion through examination under paragraph (1).
  (3) If a person listed as a candidate for promotion through examination becomes subject to disciplinary action, such as suspension from office or a more severe penalty before the promotion, the appointing authority or appointment-recommendation authority shall remove such person from the list of candidates.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

CHAPTER VI SPECIAL PROMOTION

Article 37 (Special promotion of persons of special merit) (1) Persons eligible for special promotion under Article 19 (1) 1 of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended on Jan. 6, 2017; Nov. 5, 2019; Jun. 23, 2020; Dec. 31, 2020>
  1. In cases falling under Article 40-4 (1) 1 of the State Public Officials Act: A person who has received an award under Article 35-2 (1) 1 of the Decree on the Appointment of Public Officials;
  2. In cases falling under Article 40-4 (1) 2 of the State Public Officials Act: Any of the following persons:
    (a) A person recognized by the appointing authority for significantly contributing to the advancement of police administration by improving administrative efficiency and reducing the budget;
    (b) A person who has received an award under Article 35-2 (1) 2 (b) of the Decree on the Appointment of Public Officials;
    (c) A person who has received an award determined by the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency.
  3. In cases falling under article 40-4 (1) 3 of the State Public Officials Act: A person who has received a bronze prize or higher in the grade of creation under the Citizen Suggestion Regulations and has demonstrably contributed to the advancement of police administration;
  4. In cases falling under Article 40-4 (1) 4 of the State Public Officials Act: A person who has served for at least 20 years, retired voluntarily during the period within 1 year of his or her retirement age and is deemed to have made a special contribution while in office.
  (2) Persons eligible for special promotion under Article 19 (1) 2 of the Act shall be any of the following persons: <Amended on Jul. 7, 2025>
  1. A person who was killed in action or in the line of duty equivalent thereto, or who died from injuries sustained therein, and who is recognized by the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency as having rendered distinguished service while in office;
  2. A public official who died in the line of duty as defined in Article 3 (1) 3 of the Public Officials’ Accident Compensation Act, or a public official who died in the line of duty while under danger as defined in subparagraph 4 of that paragraph, and who is recognized by the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency as having rendered distinguished service while in office.
  (3) Persons eligible for special promotion under Article 19 (1) 3 of the Act shall be as follows; in such cases, those eligible for special promotion falling under subparagraph 1, 2, or 4 shall include persons who have made a significant contribution to the resolution of cases by participating in cooperative investigations, including providing intelligence: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Nov. 19, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020; Dec. 31, 2020>
  1. A person who kills or arrests a spy or an armed communist guerrilla through dedicated efforts;
  2. A person who arrests the mastermind of a serious crime that undermines national security;
  3. A person who, through dedicated efforts, makes a special contribution to quelling violence while also enduring personal risks during wartime, accidents, or states of emergency equivalent thereto;
  4. A person who makes a particularly remarkable contribution to arresting criminals of serious crimes, such as murder, robbery, and organized violence;
  5. A person who makes a significant contribution to saving lives or protecting property in the face of natural or any other unavoidable disaster;
  6. A person who renders dedicated service in a special security department prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety and is deemed capable of performing duties at a higher position.
  (4) In cases falling under paragraph (1) 2 (b), where a person who has been awarded at least a commendation by the Prime Minister, as determined by the Minister of Personnel Management pursuant to Article 35-2 (5) of the Decree on the Appointment of Public Officials, is specially promoted, he or she may be appointed in excess of the fixed number of personnel by rank, and it shall be deemed that the relevant institution has a separate fixed number of personnel corresponding to the excess number of personnel until the current number coincides with the fixed number of personnel. In such cases, matters necessary for the procedure, operation, etc. of special promotion shall be determined by the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency. <Added on Nov. 5, 2019>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 38 (Scope of ranks of special promotion) Special promotion under Article 37 shall be limited to promotion to the following ranks: <Amended on Aug. 22, 2023>
  1. In cases falling under Article 37 (1) 1: Promotion to ranks up to Superintendent or lower;
  2. In cases falling under Article 37 (1) 2 and 3: Promotion to ranks up to Senior Inspector or lower;
  3. In cases falling under Article 37 (1) 4 or 37 (2): Promotion to ranks up to Chief Superintendent General or lower;
  4. In cases falling under Article 37 (3) 1 through 5: Promotion to ranks up to Superintendent or lower;
  5. In cases falling under Article 37 (3) 6: Promotion to ranks up to Inspector or lower.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 39 (Implementation of special promotion) The special promotion of a police official may be conducted at any time, if the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency deems it particularly necessary. <Amended on Nov. 19, 2014; Oct. 31, 2016; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 12, 2018; Jun. 23, 2020>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 40 (Exclusion from application of minimum number of service years required for promotion) (1) Article 5 (1) shall not apply to special promotions falling under Article 37 (1) 4 and (3) 2 through 5 of that Article.
  (2) Articles 5 (1) and 6 shall not apply to special promotions falling under Article 37 (2):
  (3) Articles 5 (1) and 6 (1) 4 shall not apply to special promotions falling under Article 37 (3) 1.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 40-2 (Restrictions on and revocation of special promotion) (1) A police official eligible for special promotion under Article 37 (1) 4 shall not have been subject to a severe disciplinary action or a minor disciplinary action on any of the following grounds during his or her service period:
  1. Grounds for disciplinary action under the subparagraphs of Article 78-2 (1) of the State Public Officials Act;
  2. Sexual crimes defined in Article 2 of the Act on Special Cases concerning the Punishment of Sexual Crimes;
  3. Sexual traffic defined in Article 2 (1) 1 of the Act on the Punishment of Arrangement of Commercial Sex Acts;
  4. Sexual harassment defined in subparagraph 2 of Article 3 of the Framework Act on Gender Equality;
  5. Drunk driving under Article 44 (1) of the Road Traffic Act or refusal to comply with a breath test under Article 44 (2).
  (2) If a person who has been specially promoted pursuant to Article 37 (1) 4 falls under Article 74-2 (3) 1, 1-2, or 1-3 of the State Public Officials Act and subsequently recovers honorable retirement allowances, the special promotion shall be revoked. In such cases, the person whose special promotion is revoked shall be deemed to have retired at the rank held prior to the special promotion.
  (3) Where a person specially promoted pursuant to Articles 37 (2) and 41 (1) and (2) falls under any of the following cases, the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency may revoke the relevant special promotion; provided, in cases falling under subparagraphs 1 and 3, the results of the review by the Central Promotion Review Committee shall be followed unless there is a compelling reason not to do so, and in cases falling under subparagraph 2, the relevant special promotion shall be revoked: <Added on Jul. 7, 2025>
  1. Where the Central Promotion Review Committee resolves, in its review under the latter part of Article 41 (2) on whether to ratify a special promotion, that such promotion is inappropriate;
  2. Where, in the procedure for determining benefits under the Public Officials’ Accident Compensation Act (referring to accident benefits for survivors under Article 8 (5) (b) and (c) of that Act), the Minister of Personnel Management decides not to pay such benefits on the ground that the person is not recognized as a public official who died in the line of duty as defined in Article 3 (1) 3 of that Act or as a public official who died in the line of duty while under danger as defined in subparagraph 4 of that paragraph;
  3. Where it is evident, for reasons other than subparagraph 2, that the person does not fall under any subparagraph of Article 37 (2); in such cases, the matter shall be reviewed by the Central Promotion Review Committee.
  [This Article Added on Jun. 25, 2019]

Article 41 (Special promotion review) (1) Where the appointment authority or the appointment-recommendation authority intends to specially promote police officials under his or her jurisdiction, such special promotion shall undergo a review by the Central Promotion Review Committee; provided, that where such authority intends to specially promote police officials at the rank of Inspector or below for reasons other than those prescribed in the subparagraphs of Article 37 (2), the review by the Central Promotion Review Committee may be substituted with a review by a General Promotion Review Committee, as determined by the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency. <Amended on Nov. 19, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020; Jul. 7, 2025>
  (2) Notwithstanding Article 37 (2) and paragraph (1) of this Article, where a police official has been killed in action or has died from an injury sustained in the line of duty at the scene, and it is recognized that he or she rendered distinguished service while in office, the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency may specially promote such official without undergoing review by the Central Promotion Review Committee. In such cases, the Commissioner General shall obtain ex post facto ratification from the Central Promotion Review Committee within the period prescribed in Article 35-2 (9) of the Decree on the Appointment of Public Officials. <Added on Jul. 7, 2025>
  (3) Where a person is specially promoted under paragraph (2), the Commissioner General of the Korean National Police Agency shall notify the survivors of such person that the special promotion may be revoked if ex post facto ratification is not obtained from the Central Promotion Review Committee. <Added on Jul. 7, 2025>
  (4) Where a person eligible for special promotion under Article 37 has not completed the education prescribed in subparagraph 1 of Appendix 1 of the Regulations on the Education and Training of Police Officials, he or she shall undergo a review under paragraph (1) after completing such education; provided, that this shall not apply to persons eligible for special promotion under Article 37 (1) 4, (2), or (3) 1 through 5. <Amended on Dec. 10, 2024; Jul. 7, 2025>
  (5) Matters necessary for the special promotion review under paragraph (1) shall be prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Nov. 19, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020; Jul. 7, 2025>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

Article 42 (Preparation of list of candidates for special promotion) (1) The appointing authority or the appointment-recommendation authority shall prepare a list of candidates for special promotion from those who have been selected for special promotion.
  (2) Candidates for special promotion shall be listed according to the date of the resolution on special promotion by a promotion review committee, but if multiple candidates have the same resolution date, their order of priority shall be determined by their work performance evaluation points. <Amended on Oct. 31, 2016>
  (3) Special promotions shall be conducted in the order recorded on the list of candidates for special promotion under paragraph (2), except in extenuating circumstances.
  (4) If a person listed as a candidate for special promotion becomes subject to disciplinary action of suspension from office or a more severe penalty before the promotion, the appointing authority or appointment-recommendation authority shall remove such person from the list of candidates.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

CHAPTER VII EQUIVALENT PUBLIC OFFICIALS

Article 43 (Selection of equivalent public officials) (1) The appointment authority or the appointment-recommendation authority may select, from among the police officials under his or her jurisdiction, a person who has served in the relevant rank for at least the minimum number of service years required for promotion under Article 5 and has demonstrated outstanding service performance without any grounds for restriction on promotion as an equivalent public official of the next higher rank (hereinafter referred to as "equivalent public official").
  (2) Matters necessary for the selection of equivalent public officials shall be prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Nov. 19, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017; Jun. 23, 2020>
  (3) Allowances may be paid to equivalent public officials, as prescribed by the Regulations on Allowances for Public Officials.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

CHAPTER VIII  SUPPLEMENTARY PROVISIONS

Article 44 (Processing of sensitive information and personally identifiable information) Where unavoidable to conduct the following affairs for the verification of qualifications, requirements, etc. necessary for the promotion of police officials under the Act and this Decree, the appointing authority or the appointment-recommendation authority may process information on health under Article 23 of the Personal Information Protection Act, data that constitute criminal history records under subparagraph 2 of Article 18 of the Enforcement Decree of that Act, and data containing resident registration numbers under subparagraph 1 of Article 19 of that Decree: <Amended on Dec. 20, 2022>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 9, 2013]

